@*  Names the copy before it is made.

    A duplicate is a separate workflow, and the only thing distinguishing it from its
    source in a list is its name -- so the name is asked for up front rather than left to
    be fixed afterwards, which would mean a window where two identical names are on screen
    and nobody can tell which row is which.

    The suggested name is the source's with a suffix, because the common case is a variant
    of the original rather than an unrelated workflow -- starting from the full name is
    less typing than starting from an empty box.

    Show it with a width of its own -- `new DialogOptions { MaxWidth = MaxWidth.Small,
    FullWidth = true }`. A host whose MudDialogProvider sets FullWidth without a MaxWidth
    (a reasonable thing to do for its own screens) otherwise gets this one-field form
    stretched across the display. *@

<MudDialog>
    <DialogContent>
        <MudStack Spacing="3" Style="min-width:420px">

            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mud-text-secondary">
                Copies every step, route and trigger of <b>@SourceName</b> into a new
                workflow. The copy starts as an unpublished draft, so nothing runs on it
                until you publish it, and editing it never affects the original.
            </MudText>

            <MudTextField T="string" @bind-Value="_name" Label="Name for the copy"
                          Variant="Variant.Outlined" AutoFocus="true" Immediate="true"
                          Error="@(_touched && string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_name))"
                          ErrorText="A copy needs a name of its own."
                          OnKeyDown="@OnKeyDown" />

        </MudStack>
    </DialogContent>
    <DialogActions>
        <MudButton OnClick="@(() => Dialog.Cancel())">Cancel</MudButton>
        <MudButton Color="Color.Primary" Variant="Variant.Filled"
                   Disabled="@string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_name)"
                   OnClick="Confirm">Duplicate</MudButton>
    </DialogActions>
</MudDialog>

@code {
    [CascadingParameter] private IMudDialogInstance Dialog { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>The workflow being copied. Shown, and the basis for the suggested name.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string SourceName { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    private string? _name;
    private bool _touched;

    protected override void OnInitialized() => _name = $"{SourceName} (copy)";

    private void OnKeyDown(KeyboardEventArgs args)
    {
        if (args.Key is "Enter")
        {
            Confirm();
        }
    }

    private void Confirm()
    {
        _touched = true;

        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_name))
        {
            return;
        }

        Dialog.Close(DialogResult.Ok(_name.Trim()));
    }
}
